1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:30,030
[Julio] <i>Tell me the truth, Ivy.</i>

6
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:32,365
<i>Who shot Arnaldo?!</i>

7
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>It was a man!</i>

8
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,869
<i>You were the one who shot my grandson!</i>

9
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:36,995
-[Ivy gasps]
<i>-You!</i>

10
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,872
[Diego] <i>Auntie, we had no choice.</i>
<i>Lily would've been exposed--</i>

11
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:42,333
<i>When Arnaldo wakes up, Lily's done for!</i>

12
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:46,171
<i>If she doesn't call, I'm going</i>
<i>with you to the Ardientes.</i>

13
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,881
[Ivy] <i>I'm with the Ardientes.</i>

14
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,549
<i>Don't worry. I'm safe.</i>

15
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:51,593
<i>Don't do anything that</i>
<i>might get you killed.</i>

16
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:52,761
<i>Do you understand me?</i>

17
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:55,346
[Camia] <i>Arnaldo is like</i>
<i>a ticking time bomb.</i>

18
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,265
<i>We must speed up our plans.</i>

19
00:00:57,348 --> 00:01:00,769
<i>Miss Cora is our only witness</i>
<i>against Emilia.</i>

20
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:02,687
<i>I'll sneak into her house in Sitio Nueve</i>

21
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,482
<i>and look for evidence against Emilia.</i>

22
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,484
[Raul] <i>I'm so close</i>
<i>to bringing Julio down.</i>

23
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,444
<i>So I won't give you back your title.</i>

24
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:12,238
[Damian] <i>I am the real Jaguar!</i>

25
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:16,034
<i>Tell him to give me back</i>

26
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,870
-<i>my men, my money, my weapons.</i>
-[gunshot]

27
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,747
[crowd screaming]

28
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:24,209
[Julio] <i>Either you tell me the truth</i>
<i>or you watch me unleash hell.</i>

29
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:26,127
[Ivy] <i>If you kill me,</i>

30
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:31,132
<i>it'll be like you killed</i>
<i>your only real grandson!</i>

31
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:33,551
[Julio] <i>You may have passed all the tests</i>

32
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:35,428
<i>but that doesn't mean you're off the hook.</i>

33
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,223
[man] <i>I saw two men fleeing</i>
<i>the crime scene.</i>

34
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:40,475
<i>I'll never forget their faces.</i>

35
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:43,853
[Jose] <i>It's Diego Torillo and</i>
<i>your former employee, Madrigal.</i>

36
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:47,899
-Lily.
-Mom.

37
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:49,067
[Camia] Sweetheart.

38
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:58,868
Lily, you risked your life again.

39
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:02,956
That's why I can't wait
for all this to be over.

40
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,376
Wait, you have a bruise.

41
00:02:07,043 --> 00:02:08,878
-Are you really all right?
-Mom, it's nothing.

42
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,130
It's just a bruise.

43
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:14,884
What's important is I was able
to fool the Ardientes.

44
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:18,054
I know it's hard, Mom.

45
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,348
But we have to endure for a bit more.

46
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:24,435
We're so close to ending
the Ardientes' tyranny.

47
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:26,896
Lily…

48
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:31,317
we need to send Emilia to
prison as soon as possible.

49
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:33,945
Yes, Mom.

50
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,449
But I'm still worried about you.

51
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,704
You've spent most of your life

52
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:46,124
trying to bring the Ardientes to justice.

53
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:51,838
I'm afraid that because
of what you're doing,

54
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:54,841
the wounds in your heart might never heal.

55
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,220
You never know what could happen.

56
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:02,807
You might be gone tomorrow.
And you didn't even

57
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:05,059
give yourself a chance to fall in love.

58
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:08,146
Lily…

59
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:12,775
I don't want your heart
to be filled with anger.

60
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:16,279
I don't want it to take away
your ability to love.

61
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,365
Lily, you know we love you, right?

62
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:23,411
We all do. Jepoy, Anna…

63
00:03:23,494 --> 00:03:25,330
Mom, I know.

64
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:28,207
I know that. I know that you love me.

65
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:32,086
I'm doing all this
because of my love for you.

66
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:34,923
For you, Anna, Jepoy,

67
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:38,551
Miss Loring, Mr. Pandoy,
and all the people of this town.

68
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,679
I'm doing all this for you guys.

69
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:46,684
But I love Jepoy as a friend.

70
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,728
He does everything for me.

71
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,439
He even risks his life for me.

72
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:54,692
I just hope someday, he'll meet a woman…

73
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,819
who will truly love him.

74
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,821
What about Diego?

75
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,324
Diego is part of my life.

76
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:04,410
He does everything for me too.
He's my ally.

77
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:07,664
He accepts everything about me.
He makes so many sacrifices.

78
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:10,917
He even understood
why I had to marry Arnaldo,

79
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,878
even though the thought
itself disgusted me.

80
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,922
But he's always there for me.

81
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:20,134
Mom, I have a feeling Diego
and I have a future together.

82
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:22,178
That's why I'm working hard on my plans,

83
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,222
so we can all be happy.

84
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:28,309
[sentimental music playing]

85
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,115
I'm not sure who between them
fired the gun.

86
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,617
But I'm sure of one thing.

87
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:47,203
Those two were there that night.

88
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:54,794
Colonel.

89
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,637
This is a lot of money, Congressman.

90
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,639
That's your reward.

91
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,558
I just need you to do one thing.

92
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:12,020
Don't tell anyone…

93
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:15,565
about the information you
just told me. Is that clear?

94
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:17,942
It's a promise, Congressman.

95
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:20,236
Thank you very much, Congressman.

96
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,988
-All right. You may leave.
-Go on.

97
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:23,072
Thank you.

98
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,703
What should we do about these two?

99
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:38,421
Give me the best hitmen
you can find, Colonel.

100
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:44,635
Tell them that I have
a shoot-to-kill order…

101
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:50,933
against Madrigal…

102
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:56,272
and that bastard, Diego Torillo.

103
00:05:58,274 --> 00:05:59,734
I want them dead!

104
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:01,611
I want them dead.

105
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:03,654
As in yesterday!

106
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:06,783
[tense music playing]

107
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:18,377
I'm so lucky. The congressman is the best.

108
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:19,837
[bodyguard] Keep it down.

109
00:06:20,254 --> 00:06:24,258
[ominous music playing]

110
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:44,237
I want to see Arnaldo.

111
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:51,160
Nice of you to visit him
despite what happened.

112
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:56,165
I've moved on, Congressman.

113
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:58,501
So let's forget about it.

114
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,461
What's important is…

115
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:05,091
I was able to prove my innocence.

116
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:09,178
Good.

117
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:14,058
Please take good care of him.

118
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:17,687
That's what I always do.

119
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:33,744
[suspenseful music playing]

120
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:37,415
[Anna] <i>Miss Cora is our only</i>
<i>witness against Emilia.</i>

121
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,333
[Diego] <i>I'll sneak into her</i>
<i>house in Sitio Nueve</i>

122
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:42,128
<i>and look for evidence against Emilia.</i>

123
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:43,588
[Jepoy] <i>Sitio Nueve?</i>

124
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,673
<i>Diego, the residents</i>
<i>there are pro-Ardiente.</i>

125
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:47,967
<i>If they see you, they'll mob you.</i>

126
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:05,318
Diego.

127
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,945
Anna, what are you doing here?

128
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,864
I told you I'd help, remember?

129
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:12,742
I know Cora's address too, so I came here.

130
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:15,203
We'll be in grave danger
if anyone sees you here.

131
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,245
-Now go. Go home.
-No, Diego.

132
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:17,705
I'm here now! It's too late for that.

133
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:20,416
So just let me help you. Hurry.

134
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,960
Who told you to come here?

135
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,301
Hurry.

136
00:08:31,427 --> 00:08:32,428
There.

137
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:34,972
-You got it?
-Let's move.

138
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:37,183
[door creaking]

139
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,698
Anna, be on the lookout.

140
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,367
Let me know if you see anyone approaching.

141
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:55,409
-Okay.
-Hold these.

142
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:56,577
-All right.
-Lock the door.

143
00:08:58,955 --> 00:08:59,956
I'll be quick.

144
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:16,013
[Ivy] Will you step out, please?
I want to be alone with him.

145
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:19,475
I'm sorry, ma'am,
but we can't leave the mayor.

146
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,019
Why not? On whose orders?

147
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,604
The congressman's.

148
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:38,536
[upbeat music playing]

149
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:44,041
<i>You know my secret, Arnaldo,</i>

150
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:46,502
<i>so I can't let you wake up yet.</i>

151
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:49,046
<i>I'm not done with your family.</i>

152
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:52,300
<i>I need to earn the congressman's trust</i>

153
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:57,054
<i>so I can destroy Emilia.</i>

154
00:09:57,138 --> 00:10:00,349
[upbeat music playing]

155
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:15,531
[suspenseful music playing]

156
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,633
Rudy, Kenneth, come out here!

157
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,593
Hurry! Call the cops! I saw some thieves.

158
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:37,178
[woman] Hurry!

159
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:46,646
-Guys--
-What is it?

160
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:48,481
-Victor… come out.
-What's wrong?

161
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:50,024
-I saw some thieves at Cora's place.
-Thieves?

162
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:51,400
All right. Let's go.

163
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:58,115
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,785
WOMEN'S UNION

165
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:10,169
Dexter! Hurry up!

166
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,341
Diego, the neighbors are
on their way here!

167
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,176
They're coming for us! Hurry it up there!

168
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,303
Hurry!

169
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:22,139
They're almost here!

170
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,984
Keep a close eye on that woman.

171
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:37,196
Doesn't the congressman
have other suspects in mind?

172
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:39,698
Why is he still suspicious about Aguas?

173
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,785
[Jose] The congressman
doesn't trust her at all.

174
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:45,121
So quit yapping, just do your job.

175
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:46,455
Yes, sir.

176
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:50,793
[Julio] Remember those two faces.

177
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:54,422
One million for Madrigal's body.

178
00:11:56,132 --> 00:12:00,428
And another million for Diego's corpse.

179
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,140
[Diego] Come on. Let's move.

180
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:05,474
Are you sure about what you saw?

181
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:07,560
Yeah. I saw a guy with a flashlight.

182
00:12:08,185 --> 00:12:09,979
[Diego whispers]
No. We can't get out here.

183
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:14,316
Over here. Let's go up. Come on.

184
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,901
Open the door! Move!

185
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,028
-Hurry up!
-Turn the lights on!

186
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:22,867
[Anna, hushed] Can we fit in there?

187
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:24,535
[hushed] No, it's too cramped.

188
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:27,830
They're probably out back.

189
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:29,039
Come on! Let's go.

190
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,583
[hushed] It's locked.

191
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:32,543
[Anna, hushed] There's a door there.

192
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:33,961
[Bata] Hey! There's no one here!

193
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,129
[Diego, hushed] Over here.

194
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,217
I heard something upstairs.

195
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,719
-They're upstairs!
-[whispers] Hurry!

196
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:43,387
[Bata] They're upstairs! Move!

197
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,930
-They're upstairs.
-Move, move, move!

198
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:46,348
-Move it! They might get away!
-Hurry.

199
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:48,476
-What?
-They're not here.

200
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,145
-Check over there.
-All right. Careful.

201
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,354
[door closing]

202
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:55,983
[Bata] Check that out.

203
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:00,279
[Bata] Did you find them?

204
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:07,536
Let's go.

205
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,414
-What?
-Let's go.

206
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:15,336
Diego, what do we do?

207
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:21,008
Anna, we're going to jump.

208
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:23,385
-What?
-Hold this. I'll catch you.

209
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:26,347
-Be careful. Please.
-Come on.

210
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:29,350
Anna… Anna, jump.

211
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:31,894
-Well?
-Check over there.

212
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:33,521
-It's empty.
-They're not here. It's clear.

213
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:36,273
Anna, hurry up. They might catch us. Jump!

214
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,362
[grunts] Come on.

215
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,951
I saw something. Outside.

216
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:48,869
[woman] Hey! They're outside!

217
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:49,954
-Outside?
-Let's go!

218
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:50,913
[Bata] They're outside!

219
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,918
[woman] Hurry up! We have to catch them!

220
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:00,589
-Hurry! They're outside!
-[man] Move it!

221
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,174
-Hurry up!
-Hurry up! Come on!

222
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,676
[Bata] There! Run after them! Hurry!

223
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,427
-Get them!
-Get them!

224
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,971
[woman] Hurry! We have to catch them!

225
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,598
My goodness! They got away.

226
00:14:10,474 --> 00:14:11,600
What did they steal?

227
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:12,643
Cora!

228
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:16,188
Cora, some thieves broke into your house!

229
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,189
-What?
-They broke in.

230
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,774
They got away.

231
00:14:20,901 --> 00:14:22,319
Aunt Camia, look at this.

232
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:27,074
We got that from Miss Cora's house.

233
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:32,705
Diego, Anna, these are
really important documents.

234
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:34,874
[Diego] We have to inform Ivy.

235
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,253
[phone ringing]

236
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,924
-Hello?
-[Diego] <i>Ivy.</i>

237
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:45,301
We have to meet.

238
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,428
We have some good news.

239
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,016
-All right.
-Take care.

240
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:58,814
Ivy's on her way.

241
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:02,359
She has to see these.

242
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:14,622
[phone ringing]

243
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:18,375
-Emilia?
-<i>Hello, Jaguar?</i>

244
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,044
I've been trying to call you.

245
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:22,504
Why? What's the problem?

246
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:24,924
You told me you'd do everything
for me, remember?

247
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,425
<i>Now is the time to prove that.</i>

248
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:28,552
<i>My son, Arnaldo, was shot…</i>

249
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:31,889
…and I suspect that Ivy Aguas
had something to do with it.

250
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:34,266
Make her pay for what she did to my son.

251
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:37,978
I'm sorry, Emilia, but I
can't help you this time.

252
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:39,313
Why? What's wrong?

253
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:42,274
We're on red alert.

254
00:15:43,108 --> 00:15:45,486
There's an impostor pretending to be me.

255
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:49,740
Be careful.

256
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,118
[stammers] Hello?

257
00:15:57,831 --> 00:15:59,959
-[Natalie] Hi, boys.
-Ma'am.

258
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:03,963
Hello.

259
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:06,715
Are you new here?

260
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:14,306
You look so familiar.

261
00:16:15,891 --> 00:16:17,184
What's your name again?

262
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,395
Madrigal, ma'am.

263
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:22,064
Have we met before?

264
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:23,399
Uh…

265
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,734
Actually, I was assigned
to guard you before.

266
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:27,611
I used to be Arnaldo's bodyguard.

267
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:30,030
Oh, I see.

268
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:35,869
So, why are you
on the other side of the fence?

269
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,955
I've turned my back on the Ardientes.

270
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,541
They owe me a great deal.

271
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:43,002
I know how that feels.

272
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:46,296
To be betrayed by the people you trust.

273
00:16:47,047 --> 00:16:48,048
I get it.

274
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:50,217
-[Raul] Natalie.
-Boss.

275
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:55,556
Bye.

276
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,231
Jepoy.

277
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,820
I'm glad you came.

278
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:11,363
Sit down.

279
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:19,413
Diego found some documents in Cora's house

280
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:23,417
which contain proof of Emilia's anomalies
back when she was a mayor.

281
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:33,761
Well, Attorney? Have you read
and studied all of these?

282
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:35,512
Can these help our case?

283
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,056
Yes.

284
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:40,017
But no one should be able
to prove that we stole that.

285
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,186
Otherwise, the judge won't accommodate us.

286
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:44,480
Okay. We can't afford
to make any more mistakes.

287
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:48,192
I need a strong case against Emilia.

288
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,818
Well, then, we need a whistleblower.

289
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:52,571
A witness who can confirm her corruption.

290
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:55,032
I don't think we can depend
on Cora anymore.

291
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,910
We need someone else who can help us.

292
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,163
A name made a strong impression

293
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:03,123
while I was reviewing the documents.

294
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:05,250
Divine Uytengco.

295
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:07,169
Hold on.

296
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:09,755
I've heard that name before.

297
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:15,511
I know. Emilia buys her jewelry from her.

298
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:18,972
That's right. They're friends.

299
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:21,016
[Georgina] <i>But the public doesn't know</i>

300
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:21,975
<i>about their connection.</i>

301
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:24,978
-Divine!
-Oh, my gosh, Emilia.

302
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,772
-Look at you.
-Divine.

303
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,067
-You're so sexy.
-[Emilia chuckles]

304
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,694
-I missed you.
-I missed you too, Divine.

305
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,321
Long time no see.

306
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:39,076
The truth is, most of the
money Emilia embezzles

307
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:41,912
through the foundation
goes to Divine's bank account.

308
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,374
Really?

309
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,501
So, Attorney…

310
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,546
how many millions are we talking about?

311
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:53,966
Emilia has embezzled no
less than a hundred million

312
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,592
through her foundations.

313
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:56,718
And Divine…

314
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:59,721
knows the ins and outs
of her illegal transactions.

315
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,557
So, we need her on our side.

316
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,351
Divine Uytengco.

317
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:07,187
[Divine] Oh, by the way. How's Arnaldo?

318
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,064
He's all over the news.

319
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:12,234
My gosh, Divine.
Can we not talk about him?

320
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:13,944
You know, I don't want to be depressed.

321
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:15,904
And I came here for another reason.

322
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:19,283
Why? Are you going
to upgrade your jewelry?

323
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:20,701
[chuckles] No.

324
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:23,662
I need 20 million
transferred to my account.

325
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,789
That's a lot of money, darling.

326
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:28,375
I know. But that's my own money.

327
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,877
You're just safekeeping it for me.

328
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,712
Oh, yeah. [laughs]

329
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:32,880
I need it.

330
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:37,384
Hmm. I can sense that you're
funding an electoral campaign.

331
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:40,888
Darling, that devilish smile of yours?

332
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,431
I know that so well!

333
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:44,766
You're up to no good again.

334
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,143
[Emilia laughs]

335
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:49,396
Are you running against your
own father in this election?

336
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:51,106
[both chuckle]

337
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:54,109
[sighs]

338
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,068
That's a secret.

339
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:58,071
Stay tuned for the next episode.

340
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:59,781
Cheers to that, Divine!

341
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:03,243
-I know you so well.
-It's good to see you again.

342
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:05,954
[Ivy] <i>Attorney, I want to</i>
<i>release this to the media.</i>

343
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:08,165
If we release this to the media,

344
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:10,542
Divine Uytengco will be
dragged into this mess.

345
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:12,211
Then, I'll convince her

346
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,713
to become our witness against Emilia.

347
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:18,508
Okay, Ivy. We'll take care
of exposing this to the media.

348
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:21,011
[Ivy] We need to speed up the case.

349
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:23,263
But we need a refined plan,

350
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:26,892
or else everything will go
down once Arnaldo wakes up.

351
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:29,686
What happened to the investigation
into his shooting?

352
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:32,272
The Ardientes have a new suspect.

353
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:35,067
It's just a matter of time
before they get to them.

354
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:37,861
That's why I want you all to be careful.

355
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,489
Especially you two, Diego, Jepoy.

356
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,741
[tense music playing]

357
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:50,540
I need to find out who the
Ardientes' new suspect is.

358
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:57,506
[tense music playing]

359
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:25,993
Jepoy, Anna, I'll be off. Diego.

360
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,745
-Mom.
-Lily.

361
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,417
Mom, thank you for what you're doing,

362
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:36,628
and for all your help
organizing our plans.

363
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:38,505
Lily, don't thank me.

364
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:42,009
We're doing this for Poblacion Ardiente.

365
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,845
Yes.

366
00:21:44,928 --> 00:21:46,888
You're just like your father.

367
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:49,933
He would've been so proud of you.

368
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:54,104
[instrumental theme music playing]

369
00:21:55,939 --> 00:21:57,316
I miss him so much.

370
00:22:01,695 --> 00:22:03,822
Whenever I remember Dad…

371
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:07,659
<i>I can't help but feel sad.</i>

372
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,662
<i>It still hurts.</i>

373
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:20,756
But seeing you…

374
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,342
makes me happy, Mom.

375
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:28,138
Especially now that I've
been given a second chance…

376
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:30,557
to be with you again.

377
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,601
Lily…

378
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:35,562
we'll never be apart again.

379
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:39,941
Thank you for finding me.

380
00:22:41,276 --> 00:22:42,778
For not giving up.

381
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:47,616
Lily, I love you.

382
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:50,786
I love you too, Mom.

383
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:53,580
I love you so much, Mom.

384
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:58,126
[music continues]

385
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:06,176
[exhales] We really need to
speed up our plans,

386
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:08,136
so we can make up for lost time…

387
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,138
so all this can end,

388
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:12,265
and we can both be happy together.

389
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:14,851
Always be careful out there.

390
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:16,645
You too, Mom.

391
00:23:18,855 --> 00:23:19,856
Attorney.

392
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:22,442
Take care of my mom.

393
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,027
Mom.

394
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:26,822
I'll see her out.

395
00:23:40,669 --> 00:23:42,003
The doctor said…

396
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:46,174
you'll be discharged soon.

397
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:50,595
I know, Arnaldo.

398
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:52,556
I know…

399
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:56,893
you have so many things to tell me.

400
00:23:57,727 --> 00:24:00,689
Because you saw with your own eyes…

401
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:04,192
who our real enemies are.

402
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:08,989
And I can't wait for you to wake up.

403
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:13,451
Rise and spit on the
graves of those people.

404
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,623
I will make sure

405
00:24:19,624 --> 00:24:23,211
that our kingdom is still standing
when you wake up.

406
00:24:24,045 --> 00:24:26,923
You are still my legacy.

407
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:32,220
And you will still have

408
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:34,556
a kingdom to inherit.

409
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:37,058
That is why…

410
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:41,855
I will go against Diego Torillo.

411
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:46,193
I will run for governor.

412
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:53,491
[reporter] <i>Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>
<i>has shocked the public</i>

413
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:56,203
<i>by filing his candidacy for governor.</i>

414
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:59,497
We're here now to interview
the congressman.

415
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:02,250
<i>-Congressman.</i>
<i>-Yes?</i>

416
00:25:03,210 --> 00:25:06,338
[reporter on TV]<i> Is Mayor Arnaldo</i>
<i>withdrawing his candidacy?</i>

417
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:08,048
<i>Is that why you're replacing him?</i>

418
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:11,009
[Julio on TV] <i>Are you</i>
<i>calling me a substitute?</i>

419
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:13,011
<i>Truth is…</i>

420
00:25:13,511 --> 00:25:16,598
<i>I really don't like hearing the word</i>

421
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:17,682
<i>"withdraw."</i>

422
00:25:17,766 --> 00:25:21,603
<i>In the Ardiente family,</i>
<i>I've never heard of</i>

423
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:25,982
<i>an Ardiente withdrawing from a fight.</i>

424
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:30,528
<i>It just so happens that</i>
<i>Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo</i>

425
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:33,323
<i>is recuperating.</i>

426
00:25:34,449 --> 00:25:37,327
<i>And of course, we can't turn our backs</i>

427
00:25:37,410 --> 00:25:39,079
on the people of Ardiente.

428
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:42,249
Somebody has to look after

429
00:25:42,332 --> 00:25:44,709
<i>the needs of each and every</i>
<i>one of our citizens.</i>

430
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,670
<i>Truth be told,</i>

431
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:48,797
<i>I could easily just retire</i>

432
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:51,591
<i>and enjoy the rest of my life.</i>

433
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:55,887
<i>But I'm doing this for our people.</i>

434
00:25:56,888 --> 00:25:59,891
<i>To all the people of Ardiente,</i>

435
00:25:59,975 --> 00:26:02,686
<i>who I've long considered</i>
<i>my children…</i>

436
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:08,233
<i>To all of you,</i>
<i>your Señor Julio is here once again,</i>

437
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,277
<i>asking for your help,</i>

438
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:12,028
<i>with the promise</i>

439
00:26:12,862 --> 00:26:17,909
<i>that I will never abandon you.</i>

440
00:26:19,035 --> 00:26:22,497
They'll fight tooth and claw
to hold on to their power.

441
00:26:22,580 --> 00:26:23,748
But I'll pry it from them.

442
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:29,045
Yes, they're powerful,
but more people believe in us.

443
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:33,049
No matter what happens,
we have to keep fighting.

444
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:35,343
-Fight for Diego!
-Fight for Diego!

445
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:48,690
<i>Viva Ardiente.</i>

446
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:52,777
Let's see how long your power
can protect you…

447
00:26:54,362 --> 00:26:55,864
Julio Ardiente.

448
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,118
Papa?

449
00:27:01,328 --> 00:27:03,413
You're replacing Arnaldo?

450
00:27:05,081 --> 00:27:06,958
If not me, then who?

451
00:27:07,792 --> 00:27:09,502
You? [chuckles]

452
00:27:10,170 --> 00:27:11,504
Heaven forbid.

453
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,507
[Julio laughs]

454
00:27:16,426 --> 00:27:18,219
[Ivy] From the very beginning, we knew the

455
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:21,181
Ardientes wouldn't let go of their power.

456
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,810
Diego, you need to get ready.

457
00:27:26,686 --> 00:27:29,147
I can tell that this election's

458
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:32,442
going to be dirtier and bloodier.

459
00:27:33,526 --> 00:27:37,822
Ivy, we're ready for
anything they throw at us.

460
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:44,621
Your announcement
was surprising, Congressman.

461
00:27:44,704 --> 00:27:46,498
Even I didn't expect that.

462
00:27:46,581 --> 00:27:48,875
Ivy, you should know by now

463
00:27:48,958 --> 00:27:51,753
that I am full of surprises.

464
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:54,798
I also have a couple of aces up my sleeve.

465
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:58,176
Now, what I want to know

466
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:03,598
is if I can expect your
support, Miss Ivy Aguas.

467
00:28:04,891 --> 00:28:05,809
Of course.

468
00:28:06,476 --> 00:28:08,019
Of course, Congressman.

469
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,772
Whatever support I gave to Arnaldo,

470
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:13,650
I can double…

471
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:17,278
-or triple it for you.
-Wow…

472
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:18,363
My, my.

473
00:28:18,446 --> 00:28:20,865
I'll forever be indebted

474
00:28:20,949 --> 00:28:22,742
-to you, Miss Aguas.
-[Ivy chuckles]

475
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:24,786
Thank you.

476
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:29,999
Good morning, Emilia.

477
00:28:30,417 --> 00:28:31,835
Oh, my.

478
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:34,546
It really did come true, didn't it?

479
00:28:34,629 --> 00:28:37,841
My horoscope was so right today.

480
00:28:37,924 --> 00:28:41,553
It said, "Emilia, you'll
be unlucky today."

481
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:43,388
All because I saw you!

482
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:44,514
Really?

483
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:48,059
I think your horoscope was inaccurate.

484
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:50,019
Haven't you been unlucky all your life?

485
00:28:50,103 --> 00:28:51,730
[scoffs] What are you doing here?

486
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:53,857
You're not supposed to be here.
Didn't you get the memo?!

487
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:55,567
-Don't worry, Emilia.
-Can't you read?

488
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:58,820
I just came to pick up
the stuff I left behind.

489
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:01,364
-I won't stay long.
-[scoffs]

490
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:05,201
Well, that's a relief. I can rest easy.

491
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:07,162
You know what? You should disappear.

492
00:29:07,245 --> 00:29:08,997
Evaporate. Forever!

493
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:11,207
Don't worry, I'll pray for you.

494
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:13,710
Thank you.

495
00:29:13,793 --> 00:29:17,338
I appreciate that,
although I'm shocked that…

496
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,382
you actually pray.

497
00:29:20,967 --> 00:29:26,014
Then again, you Ardientes
are good at putting up a front.

498
00:29:26,097 --> 00:29:28,057
But then…

499
00:29:28,683 --> 00:29:30,769
I think I've found my calling here.

500
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:33,229
Do you know what that calling is?

501
00:29:33,688 --> 00:29:35,982
It's to make your life miserable.

502
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:39,944
Can I go now?

503
00:29:43,948 --> 00:29:46,743
[Ivy] Oh, Jenny! Can you come with me?

504
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:50,330
[tense music playing]

505
00:30:00,298 --> 00:30:01,925
[man] All right Diego. We got this.

506
00:30:02,008 --> 00:30:04,093
-I'll leave it up to you.
-We've got this.

507
00:30:04,177 --> 00:30:07,263
Nanny, we have lots of
supporters from the other town!

508
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:08,973
-Are those ready?
-Yes, almost.

509
00:30:09,057 --> 00:30:10,558
-We still have a few here.
-Okay. Let's finish this.

510
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:11,810
-There we go.
-Good news.

511
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:13,311
Miss Cora is inside right now.

512
00:30:13,394 --> 00:30:14,229
-She is?
-Let's go.

513
00:30:14,312 --> 00:30:15,104
-Come on.
-Come on.

514
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,564
-Nanny.
-Go on. Sure.

515
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,527
-[indistinct chatter]
-My vote's for Diego.

516
00:30:20,610 --> 00:30:23,196
[ominous music playing]

517
00:30:24,989 --> 00:30:28,159
Miss, does Diego Torillo live here?

518
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:29,577
Yes. That's his place over there.

519
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:35,166
-Who was he asking about?
-Diego.

520
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:36,751
-Diego?
-Diego?

521
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:40,171
[woman] He was asking about
Diego. I wonder why…

522
00:30:41,422 --> 00:30:45,385
[tense music playing]

523
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:59,941
Jenny, you can go now. I can manage here.

524
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:39,147
Diego.

525
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:41,691
Diego, we still have a good chance.

526
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:46,404
Miss Cora, thank you
very much for joining us.

527
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:47,989
This will be a big help.

528
00:31:48,531 --> 00:31:50,325
I'm sorry for not cooperating before.

529
00:31:50,950 --> 00:31:51,951
I was just afraid.

530
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:56,664
We're sorry for what we did too.

531
00:31:56,998 --> 00:31:59,500
[motorcycle engine slowing down]

532
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:02,837
We're ready, Diego.
I've compiled all our evidence.

533
00:32:03,421 --> 00:32:05,506
I've already spoken
to my contacts in the media.

534
00:32:05,882 --> 00:32:07,133
They're waiting for us.

535
00:32:07,842 --> 00:32:10,136
-[tricycle engine starts]
-[car horn honking]

536
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:13,097
[car horn honking]

537
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:15,850
[motorcycle engine starting]

538
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:17,143
What was that?

539
00:32:19,145 --> 00:32:22,273
[car horn honking]

540
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:24,859
-Why are you blocking the way?
-I'm sorry, sir.

541
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:26,569
[man] My tricycle broke down.

542
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:28,780
[Jose] Don't you recognize
Congressman's car?

543
00:32:28,863 --> 00:32:32,325
[man] Please tell him I'm sorry
for the inconvenience.

544
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,119
Never mind. Actually,
he asked us to help you.

545
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:38,289
[ominous music playing]

546
00:32:40,541 --> 00:32:42,168
All right, boys. Help him.

547
00:32:46,089 --> 00:32:47,840
Those Ardientes will never change,

548
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:49,592
no matter what tricks they pull.

549
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:53,638
Angels by day, demons at night.

550
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:55,223
'Cause that's what they really are.

551
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:58,685
[Diego] Those people will never change.

552
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:02,522
But what's important is that
the people want change.

553
00:33:02,605 --> 00:33:05,483
Now, they know the truth
and are making a stand.

554
00:33:07,485 --> 00:33:08,528
Look at that.

555
00:33:11,197 --> 00:33:12,407
All for show.

556
00:33:13,574 --> 00:33:14,659
[sighs]

557
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:17,161
[man] Why wouldn't it break down?

558
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:18,746
The road is full of potholes.

559
00:33:20,081 --> 00:33:22,542
Because they're lining their
pockets with our tax money.

560
00:33:23,167 --> 00:33:24,711
[woman] They're even pretending to help.

561
00:33:24,794 --> 00:33:27,255
It's your fault!
You can't fool us anymore!

562
00:33:29,007 --> 00:33:32,051
Auntie. Don't lose hope.

563
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:34,804
Our sacrifices will not be in vain.

564
00:34:07,170 --> 00:34:09,922
[ominous music playing]

565
00:34:19,849 --> 00:34:22,602
Diego and Jepoy?

566
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:26,773
How did they find out?

567
00:34:33,571 --> 00:34:34,322
Auntie, excuse me.

568
00:34:34,405 --> 00:34:35,740
-Sure.
-[phone ringing]

569
00:34:35,823 --> 00:34:37,075
-[call disconnected]
-Diego.

570
00:34:39,786 --> 00:34:40,661
Is that him?

571
00:34:42,997 --> 00:34:43,748
It's him.

572
00:34:43,831 --> 00:34:46,250
-[phone ringing]
-Hello, Jepoy.

573
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:47,752
Diego, are you on your way out?

574
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:51,255
I have good news.

575
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:54,634
Miss Cora agreed to
testify against Emilia.

576
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,427
<i>She's with us right now.</i>

577
00:34:59,055 --> 00:35:01,641
-[line ringing]
-Jepoy… Jepoy, pick up.

578
00:35:01,724 --> 00:35:03,142
All right. I'll catch up with you there.

579
00:35:08,272 --> 00:35:09,315
Stop!

580
00:35:09,816 --> 00:35:10,566
[Diego] Sure.

581
00:35:11,692 --> 00:35:13,027
[Camia] Miss Cora…

582
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:16,697
thank you for changing your mind.

583
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:19,283
My conscience keeps eating at me.

584
00:35:19,367 --> 00:35:20,535
Now I want to join you.

585
00:35:20,993 --> 00:35:24,080
I'm ready to divulge Ma'am
Emilia's corrupt activities.

586
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,333
[line ringing]

587
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:28,876
[phone ringing]

588
00:35:29,335 --> 00:35:31,170
Hold on. Excuse me.

589
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:36,134
-Mom.
-Hello.

590
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:40,555
Mom… Mom, are you with Jepoy and Diego?

591
00:35:41,055 --> 00:35:43,474
Uh, just Diego. But we're on our way out…

592
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:47,228
to present the evidence against Emilia.

593
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:50,231
Mom… Mom, listen to me.

594
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:52,233
<i>Tell Diego…</i>

595
00:35:52,316 --> 00:35:55,027
that his life is in danger.
Both him and Jepoy.

596
00:35:55,111 --> 00:35:57,655
Julio has a shoot-to-kill
order against them.

597
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:03,035
Say goodbye, Diego Torillo.

598
00:36:05,371 --> 00:36:07,915
[Ivy] <i>Mom, Jepoy and Diego's lives</i>
<i>are in danger.</i>

599
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:12,211
[ominous music playing]

600
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:20,803
[gunshots]

601
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:22,471
[crowd screaming]

602
00:36:23,139 --> 00:36:24,807
-[bodyguard] Get down!
-[gunshots]

603
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:26,601
[crowd screaming]

604
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:28,603
-Get in!
-[crowd screaming]

605
00:36:28,686 --> 00:36:30,021
-[gunshots]
-[crowd screaming]

606
00:36:30,104 --> 00:36:31,856
-Hey! Come on! Move!
-[crowd screaming]

607
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:34,525
[shrieks]

608
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:35,651
-Nanny!
-Everyone, get inside!

609
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:38,029
[gunshots]

610
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:43,367
-[gunshots]
-[crowd screaming]

611
00:36:43,451 --> 00:36:46,412
Mom! Mom, talk to me. Mom!

612
00:36:46,495 --> 00:36:47,705
[gunshots]

613
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:49,207
[Georgina] Diego.

614
00:36:49,290 --> 00:36:52,210
-Miss Camia is still outside.
-[gunshots]

615
00:36:55,963 --> 00:36:56,881
[Jose] Congressman!

616
00:37:13,981 --> 00:37:14,857
Police station?

617
00:37:14,941 --> 00:37:17,610
Yes. We're here at
Mr. Diego Torillo's headquarters.

618
00:37:17,693 --> 00:37:18,819
There's a shootout outside.

619
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,780
Send policemen here and an ambulance. Now.

620
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:29,747
-Let's go in! Come on! Come on!
-Diego!

621
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:32,083
Mom!

622
00:37:36,837 --> 00:37:37,838
[grunts]

623
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:39,340
[groans]

624
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:47,265
[gunshots]

625
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,725
-[woman] Help me!
-[gunshots]

626
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:54,355
[gunshots]

627
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:55,773
-[muffled gunshot]
-Mom!

628
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:06,284
[Camia groans]

629
00:38:08,077 --> 00:38:10,913
You're a monster, Julio Ardiente!

630
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:13,291
Camia Cruz!

631
00:38:17,503 --> 00:38:19,046
Aunt Camia!

632
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:25,803
[Marlon] Diego!

633
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:27,305
<i>Diego!</i>

634
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:34,270
[Camia] <i>Lily, dear…</i>

635
00:38:39,108 --> 00:38:40,484
Auntie?

636
00:38:43,529 --> 00:38:44,655
[goon] Check if he's dead.

637
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:52,163
[grunts]

638
00:38:52,830 --> 00:38:54,165
Auntie? Aunt Camia?

639
00:38:55,541 --> 00:38:57,084
Auntie? Auntie?

640
00:38:57,168 --> 00:38:58,044
[Jose] Let's go! Let's go!

641
00:39:04,091 --> 00:39:04,925
Go!

642
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:06,427
Let's go!

643
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:20,941
Auntie? Auntie!

644
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:23,903
Help! Help! Batch!

645
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:25,488
-Camia! Camia!
-Help us!

646
00:39:25,571 --> 00:39:27,490
-Come on! Let's go!
-Camia! Camia!

647
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:28,699
-Help!
-Camia!

648
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:30,493
-Miss Camia!
-Diego.

649
00:39:31,118 --> 00:39:32,328
-The ambulance!
-Miss Camia!

650
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,955
-Help!
-Sir, hurry!

651
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:38,250
[Marlon] Open it! Get a stretcher!

652
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:40,836
-Go, Batch!
-Batch, what about our supporters?

653
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:41,879
Don't worry. I got them, Batch.

654
00:39:41,962 --> 00:39:43,631
-Help them!
-We will, Batch. Now go!

655
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:46,425
-What about the other supporters?
-Where's Cora?

656
00:39:46,509 --> 00:39:48,928
I got it. I got it. We'll help them.

657
00:39:49,011 --> 00:39:51,013
-No!
-Hold on.

658
00:39:51,472 --> 00:39:52,473
[mumbling]

659
00:39:57,686 --> 00:39:58,687
[mumbles]

660
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:01,482
No. No, no, no. No, no, Mom.

661
00:40:02,942 --> 00:40:04,610
You monsters…

662
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:19,583
Auntie. Auntie, you have to fight.

663
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:21,669
Auntie, don't leave us.

664
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:24,463
Auntie. Auntie.

665
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:26,215
[ambulance siren blaring]

666
00:40:32,638 --> 00:40:33,639
[exhales]

667
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:40,771
[somber music playing]

668
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:53,909
-[grunting]
-[ragged breathing]

669
00:41:26,817 --> 00:41:27,818
[exhales]

670
00:41:41,373 --> 00:41:42,750
[indistinct chattering]

671
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:49,465
-Ivy. Ivy.
-Let go of me.

672
00:41:49,548 --> 00:41:51,008
-Diego, let go.
-Ivy, wait.

673
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:52,551
The media are inside.

674
00:41:52,635 --> 00:41:54,345
-The Ardientes will find out!
-Let go!

675
00:41:54,762 --> 00:41:56,388
I don't care anymore!

676
00:41:57,264 --> 00:41:59,141
Ivy. Ivy. Ivy.

677
00:41:59,391 --> 00:42:01,393
-Diego!
-Ivy, stop it!

678
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:02,811
I want to see my mother!

679
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:04,605
Do you really want to see her?!

680
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:05,523
If you go in there,

681
00:42:05,606 --> 00:42:07,900
you'll be putting your mother's
life in more danger!

682
00:42:08,442 --> 00:42:10,569
All right! Go inside!

683
00:42:15,741 --> 00:42:17,743
Ivy… Ivy, I know how you feel.

684
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:20,829
But right now, we have to think clearly.

685
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:28,128
Diego, I want to see my mother.

686
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:32,174
I want to see her right now.

687
00:42:45,479 --> 00:42:48,941
Arnaldo, my son, finally you're home.

688
00:42:49,858 --> 00:42:53,070
It's safer for him here at
home than at the hospital.

689
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,989
At least here, he'll be with us.

690
00:42:55,739 --> 00:42:59,618
And I believe he can
recover faster if he's here.

691
00:43:00,202 --> 00:43:02,788
You are so right, Papa.
I'm gonna take care of my son.

692
00:43:02,871 --> 00:43:05,165
Come on, let's take him inside. Hurry.

693
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:07,334
[Emilia] Be careful, okay?

694
00:43:08,544 --> 00:43:10,004
Careful now.

695
00:43:10,087 --> 00:43:11,463
Let's go to our office.

696
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:22,141
[foreboding music playing]

697
00:43:27,229 --> 00:43:28,314
[bodyguard] Move aside. Go on.

698
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:29,565
Let them through.

699
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:34,945
-Sir.
-Move aside! Let me through!

700
00:43:35,029 --> 00:43:36,947
[woman] My son! Let me through! My son!

701
00:43:39,074 --> 00:43:40,492
Doc, what happened to my son?

702
00:43:42,953 --> 00:43:44,163
[woman] Doc! Doc!

703
00:43:50,794 --> 00:43:54,423
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

704
00:43:56,550 --> 00:43:57,551
[Ivy sobs]

705
00:43:58,844 --> 00:44:02,431
Mom. Mom. Mom.

706
00:44:07,186 --> 00:44:09,521
Mom, I'm sorry.

707
00:44:17,738 --> 00:44:19,073
Mom.

708
00:44:20,949 --> 00:44:22,826
Mom, I'm sorry. You got dragged into this.

709
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:23,952
Mom.

710
00:44:26,872 --> 00:44:29,375
[Ivy weeping]

711
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:44,682
[sentimental music playing]

712
00:44:45,933 --> 00:44:46,850
Mom?

713
00:44:49,687 --> 00:44:53,232
[monitor beeping rapidly]

714
00:44:53,315 --> 00:44:54,483
[steady beep]

715
00:44:54,566 --> 00:44:56,193
-Aunt Camia?
-Mom?

716
00:44:56,652 --> 00:44:57,694
-Camia.
-Mom, no.

717
00:44:57,778 --> 00:44:58,987
-Auntie!
-Mom! No!

718
00:44:59,071 --> 00:44:59,905
-Mom!
-Doc!

719
00:44:59,988 --> 00:45:00,739
-Mom! Mom!
-Doc!

720
00:45:00,823 --> 00:45:02,366
Mom! Mom, no, no, no!

721
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:03,492
-Nurse.
-Mom, no!

722
00:45:03,575 --> 00:45:07,454
-Excuse me, ma'am.
-Mom, come on. Mom!

723
00:45:07,538 --> 00:45:10,999
Mom! Mom, don't leave me. Mom!

724
00:45:11,083 --> 00:45:13,127
Check the vital signs.

725
00:45:13,210 --> 00:45:16,338
Mom! Mom! No! No! No!

726
00:45:21,927 --> 00:45:22,928
No!

727
00:45:23,846 --> 00:45:27,474
Mom! Mom! No!

728
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:29,685
[nurse] Excuse me, ma'am.
You can't be here.

729
00:45:29,768 --> 00:45:31,603
-Please revive my mom.
-I have to ask you to step out.

730
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:34,189
Revive my mom, Miss. Please!
Please help her!

731
00:45:35,232 --> 00:45:36,483
[Ivy sobbing]

732
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:38,735
Our hitmen were able to ambush Madrigal.

733
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:40,821
But he got away.

734
00:45:44,741 --> 00:45:46,243
What about Diego?

735
00:45:49,204 --> 00:45:50,330
Diego is alive.

736
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:52,541
But many of his supporters got hurt.

737
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:57,296
And Camia Cruz?

738
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:00,174
There's no confirmation yet.

739
00:46:00,257 --> 00:46:01,967
We're waiting to hear
if she's dead or alive.

740
00:46:02,050 --> 00:46:03,343
Well…

741
00:46:03,427 --> 00:46:07,055
make sure Diego knows…

742
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:10,726
he was the target of that ambush.

743
00:46:11,894 --> 00:46:14,104
That way he'll know he's responsible

744
00:46:14,188 --> 00:46:16,315
for what happened to his supporters.

745
00:46:16,398 --> 00:46:17,357
Yes, sir.

746
00:46:19,776 --> 00:46:20,569
Ma'am.

747
00:46:25,491 --> 00:46:28,494
Papa? You issued an order to kill Diego?

748
00:46:29,661 --> 00:46:31,872
Diego and Madrigal.

749
00:46:32,414 --> 00:46:35,209
Because I suspect that those two
are the ones who shot Arnaldo.

750
00:46:36,376 --> 00:46:37,544
But you know, Papa?

751
00:46:37,628 --> 00:46:39,796
The little things
that you do for the family?

752
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:42,090
Makes me proud to be an Ardiente.

753
00:46:43,926 --> 00:46:45,844
Viva Ardiente, Papa.

754
00:46:46,762 --> 00:46:48,222
Viva Ardiente.

755
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,682
That was a really good one, Papa.

756
00:46:51,892 --> 00:46:53,268
Bold move.

757
00:46:58,857 --> 00:47:00,984
[Ivy] Make sure the whole
hospital is secured.

758
00:47:01,068 --> 00:47:02,819
Don't worry. I'll take care of everything.

759
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:04,279
-Yes, ma'am.
-Thank you.

760
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:17,417
Who shot my mother?

761
00:47:18,710 --> 00:47:22,548
[tense music playing]

762
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:25,259
Julio Ardiente.

763
00:47:25,342 --> 00:47:28,512
[tense music continues]

764
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,474
[growls]

765
00:47:35,018 --> 00:47:37,020
Julio, you bastard.

766
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:48,907
[suspenseful music swelling]

767
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:56,790
[Julio] <i>Jaguar was the one</i>
<i>who tried to kill your son.</i>

768
00:47:56,873 --> 00:47:58,208
<i>You betrayed me!</i>

769
00:47:58,292 --> 00:48:00,002
<i>That's the gun I gave Madrigal.</i>

770
00:48:00,085 --> 00:48:02,212
<i>He probably did that for personal reasons.</i>

771
00:48:02,296 --> 00:48:04,006
<i>Then kill Madrigal!</i>

772
00:48:04,089 --> 00:48:06,216
<i>We now know who did it.</i>

773
00:48:06,300 --> 00:48:07,968
<i>I assume you feel guilty</i>

774
00:48:08,051 --> 00:48:10,304
<i>for all the other people you've hurt.</i>

775
00:48:10,387 --> 00:48:14,725
<i>They deserved every bullet</i>
<i>that flew all over that place!</i>

776
00:48:14,808 --> 00:48:16,476
[Ivy] <i>So, it's Madrigal.</i>

777
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:18,520
[Julio] <i>And he is about to die.</i>

778
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:20,731
<i>He will definitely pay for this!</i>

779
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:23,609
<i>Come with me.</i>

780
00:48:24,401 --> 00:48:26,987
[theme music playing]
